["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Read what a bear is telling you and you will know when to wait, when to back off, and when to shoot.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Black bear body language from calm to dangerous. Unaware: feeding, head down; watch and plan. Aware: stands, sniffs, stares; freeze and let it settle. Stressed: huffs, jaw pops, swats the ground; it wants space, back off. Bluff charge: runs in and stops short; stand your ground with spray ready. Stalking you: quiet and keeps coming; spray, then fight back. From WildSafeBC and BC bear safety guidance.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Read the bear: calm to dangerous</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"50\" width=\"10\" height=\"42\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"24\" y=\"50\" width=\"366\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Unaware</text><text x=\"32\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Feeding, head down</text><text x=\"382\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Watch. Plan.</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"99\" width=\"10\" height=\"42\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"24\" y=\"99\" width=\"366\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"117\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Aware</text><text x=\"32\" y=\"135\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Stands, sniffs, stares</text><text x=\"382\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Freeze. Let it settle.</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"148\" width=\"10\" height=\"42\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"24\" y=\"148\" width=\"366\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\">Stressed</text><text x=\"32\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Huffs, jaw pops, swats</text><text x=\"382\" y=\"175\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">It wants space. Back off.</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"197\" width=\"10\" height=\"42\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"24\" y=\"197\" width=\"366\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"215\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\">Bluff charge</text><text x=\"32\" y=\"233\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Runs in, stops short</text><text x=\"382\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Stand. Spray ready.</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"246\" width=\"10\" height=\"42\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#b02a2a\"/><rect x=\"24\" y=\"246\" width=\"366\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#b02a2a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#b02a2a\" text-anchor=\"start\">Stalking you</text><text x=\"32\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Quiet, keeps coming</text><text x=\"382\" y=\"273\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Spray, then fight back.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Most black bears avoid people <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Huffs, jaw pops, stomps: it wants space <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this chapter covers</summary><ul><li>Body language and alarm signals, flight, sows and cubs, boars, home ranges, learning and memory, predictable habits, and bear safety with spray.</li><li>Full safety lesson: <a href=\"#/s/bear-cougar-encounters\">Bears and cougars</a>.</li><li>Previous: <a href=\"#/s/mc-black-bear-03\">Chapter 3, The senses</a>. Next: <a href=\"#/s/mc-black-bear-05\">Chapter 5, The year</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A bear telling you to back off: jaw popping, woofing, moaning, stomping, a bluff charge that stops short, ears back and head low. It is stressed and defensive. Give it room.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A bear telling you: back off</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"112\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff3d6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"76\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jaw popping</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">teeth clacking</text><rect x=\"145\" y=\"48\" width=\"112\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff3d6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"201\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Woofing</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">loud huffs</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"48\" width=\"112\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff3d6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"326\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Moaning</text><text x=\"326\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">low sound</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"144\" width=\"112\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff3d6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"76\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stomping</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">paws slap</text><rect x=\"145\" y=\"144\" width=\"112\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff3d6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"201\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bluff charge</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">runs, stops short</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"144\" width=\"112\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff3d6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"326\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ears back</text><text x=\"326\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">head low</text><rect x=\"41\" y=\"254\" width=\"317\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"275\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stressed, defensive. Give it room</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Jaw popping, woofing, moaning, stomping, a bluff charge <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>A stressed, defensive bear. Give it room <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: alarm signals in detail</summary><ul><li>WildSafeBC lists the agitated bear signs: \"jaw popping, moaning, woofing, stomping the ground, or a bluff charge\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Speak calmly, back away, avoid direct eye contact, ready your spray.</li><li>A woof or huff from a sow is often the signal that sends cubs up a tree (Tip, next screens).</li><li>Ears laid back and head low go with stress (Tip, <a href=\"#/s/bear-cougar-encounters\">bear safety</a>).</li><li>Standing up is curiosity, not attack (Tip, chapter 3).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Defensive or predatory attack. Defensive: the bear was surprised or is protecting cubs or food, it comes fast and noisy from close; spray, and if it makes contact, lie flat and still. Predatory: the bear sees you as food, it is quiet, stalks and keeps coming; spray and fight back hard. Cougar: always fight back.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Attack: defensive or predatory?</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"46\" width=\"100\" height=\"50\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#c9c2ad\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\"></text><rect x=\"110\" y=\"46\" width=\"140\" height=\"50\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#c9c2ad\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Defensive</text><rect x=\"250\" y=\"46\" width=\"140\" height=\"50\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#c9c2ad\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Predatory</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"96\" width=\"100\" height=\"50\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#c9c2ad\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Why</text><rect x=\"110\" y=\"96\" width=\"140\" height=\"50\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#c9c2ad\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Surprised, cubs,</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">food</text><rect x=\"250\" y=\"96\" width=\"140\" height=\"50\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#c9c2ad\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sees you</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">as food</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"146\" width=\"100\" height=\"50\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3efe2\" stroke=\"#c9c2ad\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Looks like</text><rect x=\"110\" y=\"146\" width=\"140\" height=\"50\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3efe2\" stroke=\"#c9c2ad\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fast, noisy,</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">from close</text><rect x=\"250\" y=\"146\" width=\"140\" height=\"50\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3efe2\" stroke=\"#c9c2ad\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Quiet, stalks,</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">keeps coming</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"196\" width=\"100\" height=\"50\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#c9c2ad\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text><rect x=\"110\" y=\"196\" width=\"140\" height=\"50\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#c9c2ad\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Spray. Contact:</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">lie flat, still</text><rect x=\"250\" y=\"196\" width=\"140\" height=\"50\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#c9c2ad\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Spray. Fight</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">back hard</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"285\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cougar: always fight back</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Fatal black bear attacks in BC: under 1 every 3 years <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Dogs were part of over half of injuries in one review <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what a bear does when disturbed</summary><ul><li>Most black bears that notice a person leave, often fast and quietly (Tip, hunter consensus).</li><li>A defensive bear (surprised, guarding cubs or food) comes noisy and fast; a predatory bear is quiet, stalks and keeps coming (75%, WildSafeBC, <a href=\"#/s/bear-cougar-encounters\">bear safety</a>).</li><li>WildSafeBC: fatal black bear attacks average less than one every three years in BC <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Hristienko and Herrero (2014) found dogs involved in over 50% of black bear injuries to people (70%, via WildSafeBC).</li><li>A gut pile or a kill draws bears, which may then defend it (75%, <a href=\"#/s/bear-cougar-encounters\">bear safety</a>).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: a black bear sow stands in the open. She gives an alarm woof and her two cubs run to a tree and climb it while she stays near the base. Cubs in a tree mean a sow is close: a bear under 2 years old, and any bear with it, is never legal.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sow woofs, cubs climb</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"250\" width=\"400\" height=\"50\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"300\" y=\"60\" width=\"16\" height=\"190\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M308 40 L270 120 L346 120 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M308 90 L262 180 L354 180 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" opacity=\".85\"/><g transform=\"translate(150 215) scale(0.9 0.9)\"><rect x=\"-38\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><rect x=\"-26\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><rect x=\"24\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><rect x=\"34\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M-46 6 Q-52 -28 -24 -30 Q0 -26 26 -22 Q46 -18 46 4 Q30 24 -30 22 Q-46 20 -46 6 Z\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M40 -20 L62 -16 L78 -8 Q82 -2 76 0 L56 4 Q44 2 40 -20 Z\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M48 -18 L50 -32 L56 -18 Z\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M66 -10 L78 -8 Q82 -2 76 0 L64 -2 Z\" fill=\"#8b6a4a\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#eee\"/></g><g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.32 0.32)\"><rect x=\"-38\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#3a2a1c\"/><rect x=\"-26\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#3a2a1c\"/><rect x=\"24\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#3a2a1c\"/><rect x=\"34\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#3a2a1c\"/><path d=\"M-46 6 Q-52 -28 -24 -30 Q0 -26 26 -22 Q46 -18 46 4 Q30 24 -30 22 Q-46 20 -46 6 Z\" fill=\"#3a2a1c\"/><path d=\"M40 -20 L62 -16 L78 -8 Q82 -2 76 0 L56 4 Q44 2 40 -20 Z\" fill=\"#3a2a1c\"/><path d=\"M48 -18 L50 -32 L56 -18 Z\" fill=\"#3a2a1c\"/><path d=\"M66 -10 L78 -8 Q82 -2 76 0 L64 -2 Z\" fill=\"#8b6a4a\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#eee\"/></g><animateMotion path=\"M230 232 L290 232 L292 120\" dur=\"2.5s\" begin=\"0.8s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.32 0.32)\"><rect x=\"-38\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#3a2a1c\"/><rect x=\"-26\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#3a2a1c\"/><rect x=\"24\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#3a2a1c\"/><rect x=\"34\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#3a2a1c\"/><path d=\"M-46 6 Q-52 -28 -24 -30 Q0 -26 26 -22 Q46 -18 46 4 Q30 24 -30 22 Q-46 20 -46 6 Z\" fill=\"#3a2a1c\"/><path d=\"M40 -20 L62 -16 L78 -8 Q82 -2 76 0 L56 4 Q44 2 40 -20 Z\" fill=\"#3a2a1c\"/><path d=\"M48 -18 L50 -32 L56 -18 Z\" fill=\"#3a2a1c\"/><path d=\"M66 -10 L78 -8 Q82 -2 76 0 L64 -2 Z\" fill=\"#8b6a4a\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#eee\"/></g><animateMotion path=\"M255 236 L304 236 L306 150\" dur=\"2.5s\" begin=\"1.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><text x=\"150\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">woof!</text><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1;1;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.1;0.8;1\" begin=\"0.3s\" dur=\"2s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"262\" width=\"380\" height=\"32\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cubs in a tree mean: never shoot the sow.</text><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"4.2s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Sow woofs, cubs climb. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Sow with cubs is never legal <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Cubs often climb when alarmed; she stays near (Tip).</li></ul><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-bb-sow-cubs.jpg\" alt=\"Black bear sow with two cubs, one black and one cinnamon, Yellowstone. Colour phases mix in one family. Cubs and sows with cubs are protected in BC (VERIFY page).\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Black bear sow with two cubs, one black and one cinnamon, Yellowstone. Colour phases mix in one family. Cubs and sows with cubs are protected in BC (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> page). <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Neal Herbert, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Black_bear_with_cubs_(772a9ae1-a841-4d01-910a-484d8842cda0).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: family life in detail</summary><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><ul><li>Black bears are \"mostly solitary. The only common social groups are the sow with her cubs and the mating pair\" (90%, BC account).</li><li>Cubs stay with the mother their whole first year, den with her, and leave by the middle or end of the second spring when she drives them off to breed again <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>She \"protects them and teaches them how to survive\" <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>. Daughters may set up ranges that overlap hers; sons disperse <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Females with cubs avoid open areas when moving between feeding sites (90%, BC account). So a sow may feed at the edge while cubs wait in cover (Tip).</li><li>Item 14, page 11: no bear under 2 and no bear in its company (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-unlawful-acts\">unlawful acts</a>).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Circles drawn to scale: an adult male black bear home range is typically 25 to 150 square kilometres, a female 5 to 25 square kilometres, from the BC government account. Big males roam widely; a sow stays in a smaller area.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Home range: boar vs sow (to scale)</text><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"170\" r=\"100\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".18\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"170\" r=\"41\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".35\"/><circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"200\" r=\"41\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" opacity=\".45\"/><circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"200\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" opacity=\".8\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Boar 25 to 150 km2</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sow 5 to 25 km2</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Big males roam; a sow stays put (90%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Boars roam 25 to 150 km2; sows 5 to 25 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Big boars rub trees and push smaller bears off food <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: boars in detail</summary><ul><li>Home range \"of adult males, typically 25 to 150 km2, are larger than those of females, which vary from 5 to 25 km2\" (90%, BC account).</li><li>Mating season, early June to mid July: boars travel widely looking for sows (90% timing; Tip on travel).</li><li>Boone and Crockett (Jim Shockey): boar behaviours include rubbing on trees, straddling and breaking saplings, chasing other bears and dominating smaller bears; big bears hold the best habitat at prime feeding times; small bears stay near escape trees <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Adult males sometimes kill cubs (sexually selected infanticide); sows with young cubs avoid males in mating season. In an Alberta study of hunted black bears the effect on numbers was weak <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>An old boar is the bear most likely to feed only at last light or at night where people are (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: a black bear feeds in a berry patch above you. At first the wind blows from the bear toward you, so your scent cone trails behind you, away from the bear. Then the wind swings around and your scent cone swings toward the bear. The bear lifts its head: it smells you. Check the wind before every move.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".6\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Your scent rides the wind</text><g transform=\"translate(120 92) scale(1.2)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-2\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"-2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-16\" cy=\"4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"4\" cy=\"5\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(250 84) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-2\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"-2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-16\" cy=\"4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"4\" cy=\"5\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(320 110) scale(1)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-2\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"-2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-16\" cy=\"4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"4\" cy=\"5\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(200 100)\"><g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.7 0.7)\"><rect x=\"-38\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><rect x=\"-26\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><rect x=\"24\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><rect x=\"34\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M-46 6 Q-52 -28 -24 -30 Q0 -26 26 -22 Q46 -18 46 4 Q30 24 -30 22 Q-46 20 -46 6 Z\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M40 -20 L62 -16 L78 -8 Q82 -2 76 0 L56 4 Q44 2 40 -20 Z\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M48 -18 L50 -32 L56 -18 Z\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M66 -10 L78 -8 Q82 -2 76 0 L64 -2 Z\" fill=\"#8b6a4a\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#eee\"/></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0;0;-10\" keyTimes=\"0;0.9;1\" begin=\"0s\" dur=\"6s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g></g><g transform=\"translate(200 250)\"><g><path d=\"M0 0 L-50 70 L50 70 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".22\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0;0;180\" keyTimes=\"0;0.55;0.8\" dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"6\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\">You</text></g><g stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><g><path d=\"M40 60 v40 m-6 -10 l6 10 l6 -10 M360 60 v40 m-6 -10 l6 10 l6 -10\" fill=\"none\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0 200 150;0 200 150;180 200 150\" keyTimes=\"0;0.55;0.8\" dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g></g><g><text x=\"20\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">Wind: bear to you. Good.</text><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;1;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.5;0.6\" dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"140\" width=\"250\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"163\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Wind swung. Bear smells you.</text><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>The lesson a bear learns fastest: your smell. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Big brain for its size; excellent long term memory <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Learns where food and danger are, and when (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: learning in detail</summary><ul><li>North American Bear Center: bears have a large brain for their body size and excellent long term memory; navigation better than ours <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Bears that learn garbage, fruit trees or coolers return to them; conflict bears are often destroyed (90%, BC account).</li><li>Near people, bears shift feeding to night (75%, WildSafeBC; 65%, a Massachusetts GPS (Global Positioning System) collar study).</li><li>Pressure: a bear that is bumped at a berry patch may switch to dark only use of it (Tip). Disturb a feeding area once, then leave it alone (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Habit</th><th>Use it</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Follows the richest food in season <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span></td><td>Hunt the food, not the bear</td></tr><tr><td>Steps in the same prints on old trails <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span></td><td>Find worn trails near food</td></tr><tr><td>Uses cover between feeding sites <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span></td><td>Watch the edge where cover meets food</td></tr><tr><td>Comes back to a good food source (Tip)</td><td>Glass it again at the same hour</td></tr><tr><td>Feeding bear is noisy, focused (Tip)</td><td>Move while it feeds</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the sources for the habits</summary><ul><li>BC account <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>: bears \"seek out concentrated food sources such as spawning fish and dense berry patches\"; \"home ranges are usually made up of several feeding areas connected by travel routes... often located in wooded areas that provide cover\"; bears \"often step in the same footprints of other bears, thus creating well worn paths that they use year after year\".</li><li>The rest are hunting tips, not measured facts.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: a bear comes toward you. Aim the spray at the ground a few metres in front of the bear, then sweep up to its face. The orange cloud forms a wall the bear runs into. Never spray into the wind.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bear spray: low, then sweep up</text>\n  <rect y=\"210\" width=\"400\" height=\"90\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"150\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"164\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"210\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n  <line x1=\"52\" y1=\"174\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"176\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"78\" y=\"168\" width=\"16\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <g>\n    <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"60 0;0 0\" dur=\"5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"320\" cy=\"180\" rx=\"44\" ry=\"28\" fill=\"#2f2a26\"/><circle cx=\"278\" cy=\"166\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#2f2a26\"/><circle cx=\"272\" cy=\"150\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#2f2a26\"/>\n    <rect x=\"290\" y=\"196\" width=\"12\" height=\"18\" fill=\"#2f2a26\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"196\" width=\"12\" height=\"18\" fill=\"#2f2a26\"/>\n  </g>\n  <path d=\"M96 180 L250 206 L250 160 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0\">\n    <animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;.55;.55\" keyTimes=\"0;0.2;1\" begin=\"1s\" dur=\"3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <animate attributeName=\"d\" values=\"M96 180 L230 214 L230 196 Z;M96 180 L230 214 L230 196 Z;M96 180 L240 200 L240 140 Z\" keyTimes=\"0;0.4;1\" begin=\"1s\" dur=\"3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n  </path>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1;1;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.1;0.8;1\" begin=\"1s\" dur=\"1.6s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1. Aim at the ground</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"2.6s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2. Sweep up to the face</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"4.5s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"60\" y=\"262\" width=\"280\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"283\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Never spray into the wind</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Aim low, sweep up. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Spray when the bear is about 5 to 10 m away <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Spray stopped black bears about 90% of the time in Alaska <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bear spray by distance, from Alberta bear safety guidance: 9 to 15 metres, a half to 1 second warning blast aimed slightly down. 6 to 9 metres, 1 to 2 second bursts aimed low in front of the head. 0 to 6 metres, bursts at the head. Keep some in reserve, then back away while watching the bear.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bear spray by distance</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"200\" width=\"400\" height=\"100\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><line x1=\"33\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"36\" y2=\"174\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"6.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"47\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"44\" y2=\"174\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"6.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"30\" y=\"148\" width=\"20\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"31\" y1=\"153\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"172\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"5.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"49\" y1=\"153\" x2=\"56\" y2=\"172\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"5.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"140\" r=\"9.0\" fill=\"#d9b48f\"/><rect x=\"60\" y=\"206\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0 to 6 m</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">At the head</text><rect x=\"160\" y=\"206\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6 to 9 m</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bursts, aim low</text><rect x=\"260\" y=\"206\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f6c344\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">9 to 15 m</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Warning blast</text><ellipse cx=\"360\" cy=\"180\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#2f2a26\"/><circle cx=\"334\" cy=\"174\" r=\"10.2\" fill=\"#2f2a26\"/><circle cx=\"336\" cy=\"164\" r=\"3.6\" fill=\"#2f2a26\"/><circle cx=\"324\" cy=\"176\" r=\"4.2\" fill=\"#2f2a26\"/><rect x=\"342\" y=\"190\" width=\"7\" height=\"10\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#2f2a26\"/><rect x=\"372\" y=\"190\" width=\"7\" height=\"10\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#2f2a26\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1 to 2 second bursts</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">keep some in reserve</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Then back away, watching it</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: spray and safety in detail</summary><ul><li>WildSafeBC: carry spray where you can reach it fast, use it at about 5 to 10 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Smith, Herrero and others (2008), Alaska incidents 1985 to 2006: spray stopped undesirable behaviour in 92% of brown bear, 90% of black bear and 100% of polar bear cases; 98% of people with spray were uninjured in close encounters; wind interfered in 5 of 71 cases (80%, journal abstract via search preview). Only 20 black bear cases: a small sample (Tip).</li><li>Spray versus firearms: see <a href=\"#/s/bear-cougar-encounters\">bear safety</a> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Defensive contact: lie on your stomach, hands over the back of your neck, legs apart. Predatory attack: fight back at the face (75%, WildSafeBC).</li><li>Hunters are at higher risk than hikers: quiet, early, late, in thick cover, with a carcass (75%, <a href=\"#/s/bear-cougar-encounters\">bear safety</a>).</li><li>Bear bells: WildSafeBC does not recommend them <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul></details><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aIvpLzHiCrg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>How to Use Bear Spray - Banff National Park</b><small>Remove the clip, aim low, spray a cloud between you and the bear.<br>Parks Canada, YouTube, 2 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A bear telling you to back off: jaw popping, woofing, moaning, stomping, a bluff charge that stops short, ears back and head low. It is stressed and defensive. Give it room.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A bear telling you: back off</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"112\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff3d6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"76\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jaw popping</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">teeth clacking</text><rect x=\"145\" y=\"48\" width=\"112\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff3d6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"201\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Woofing</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">loud huffs</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"48\" width=\"112\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff3d6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"326\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Moaning</text><text x=\"326\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">low sound</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"144\" width=\"112\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff3d6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"76\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stomping</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">paws slap</text><rect x=\"145\" y=\"144\" width=\"112\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff3d6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"201\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bluff charge</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">runs, stops short</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"144\" width=\"112\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff3d6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"326\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ears back</text><text x=\"326\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">head low</text><rect x=\"41\" y=\"254\" width=\"317\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"275\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stressed, defensive. Give it room</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Pop and woof, give it room; quiet and coming, spray it soon.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 5 to 10: metres to spray <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. 90: percent of black bear cases stopped <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (opinion, the quick lesson, built on the synopsis \"Be patient\"): \"Watch a bear five minutes. Cubs show up in the fourth.\"</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 25 to 150 and 5 to 25: boar and sow home ranges in km2 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Cubs up a tree, sow close by: keep your safety on, walk on by.\"</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (opinion, the synopsis notice): \"Be patient. Don't shoot the moment you see a bear.\"</li></ul><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Thinking a woofing, jaw popping bear is about to attack. It is warning you.</li><li>Carrying spray in the pack.</li><li>Bringing a loose dog into bear country.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Practise with an inert spray can: draw, safety clip off, fire low, 10 times.</p></aside></details>","<ul><li>BC Ministry of Environment, Lands and Parks (2001), <a href=\"https://www.env.gov.bc.ca/wld/documents/blackbear.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\"Black Bears in British Columbia\"</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span></li></ul><ul><li>WildSafeBC, <a href=\"https://wildsafebc.com/species/black-bear/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Black bear</a>, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Smith, Herrero, DeBruyn and Wilder (2008), <a href=\"https://bioone.org/journals/journal-of-wildlife-management/volume-72/issue-3/2006-452/Efficacy-of-Bear-Deterrent-Spray-in-Alaska/10.2193/2006-452.full\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\"Efficacy of Bear Deterrent Spray in Alaska\"</a>, Journal of Wildlife Management 72(3), search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Boone and Crockett Club, <a href=\"https://boone-crockett.org/node/621\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Field judging black bear</a> (Jim Shockey), checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li></ul><ul><li>North American Bear Center, <a href=\"https://bear.org/?p=53\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Senses and abilities</a>, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Czetwertynski and others, Alberta black bear sexually selected infanticide study, Ursus, search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li></ul>","<ul><li>Massachusetts black bear GPS (Global Positioning System) study, secondary write up, search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Hunt Mentor: <a href=\"#/s/bear-cougar-encounters\">Bears and cougars</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-unlawful-acts\">unlawful acts</a> (as marked there)</li></ul><ul><li>Research notes: <code>research/2026-10-11-masterclass-black-bear.md</code>.</li></ul>"]